WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Superficial Musculature of the Back & Posterior Trunk.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The superficial extrinsic back muscles connect the axial skeleton (vertebral column) to the appendicular skeleton of the upper limb.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Trapezius: Expansive flat diamond-shaped muscle originating from external occipital protuberance to T12 spinous processes, innervated by spinal accessory nerve (CN XI).

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Latissimus dorsi: Broad triangular muscle of the lower back, inserting into the floor of the bicipital groove of the humerus.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Deep to trapezius lie levator scapulae and rhomboids (major and minor), innervated by the dorsal scapular nerve (C5).
